# 2. Client sends: length-prefixed (8-byte big-endian) secret file contents  
# 3. Server sends: length-prefixed version string
# 4. Client sends: length-prefixed CBOR-encoded message
# 5. Server sends: length-prefixed CBOR-encoded response
#
# The messages are CBOR-encoded Rust enums (serde with CBOR)
# 
# Now I understand this is using the `ciborium` or `serde_cbor` crate in Rust.
#
